  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically screened for acute danger symptoms (RC1), correctly framed the case around obstructive sleep-disordered breathing (RC2), clarified preoperative information gaps (RC3), and safely handled coagulation test boundaries (RC4). The conversation extended over 25 turns covering preoperative waiting, intraoperative support, and postoperative discharge planning, achieving safe executable closure with caregiver teach-back. No serious or minor responsibility-chain errors were found. Two high-order points (HO1 plain-language caregiver communication with checklist teach-back, HO2 family conflict and fatigue navigation) were actively and completely triggered, evidenced by the doctor's structured, plainly worded, prioritized instructions adapted to a worried, moderately health-literate parent and by the practical family meeting and question-list workflow. HO3 and HO4 were also triggered and partially or completely addressed. Therefore, the trajectory satisfies Strong and Perfect criteria with no in-chain error and at least two completed high-order points.",
